@meta
id: 17-04
title: Drill — out, fix, back, dot
chapter: 17
type: drill
skills: jump-back
par: 28
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: F2 rename, which is fair, but it does not exist in a log or a markdown file
open: retry.config.ts

@brief
Eight times: `MAX_RETRIES` is declared on line 1 and used once at the
bottom. Rename both to `RETRY_LIMIT`. Start from the declaration, jump
to the use, change it, come back, and let the dot command change the
one you are standing on.

Two changes, one typed. The rhythm you are after is star, change,
`Ctrl-O`, dot.

@keys
| `*` | jump to the next occurrence of the word under the cursor |
| `ciw` | change the word |
| `Ctrl-O` | back to where `*` started, exact column |
| `.` | repeat the change |

@hints
`2w` gets you onto `MAX_RETRIES` from the start of line 1. `*` is a
jump, so `Ctrl-O` knows the way back.
--
`Ctrl-O` returns you to the same character `*` left from, which is
inside the word, which is all `.` needs to repeat `ciw`.

@solution
    2w * ciwRETRY_LIMIT<Esc> Ctrl-O . :wq<Enter>

Twenty-four keystrokes, eleven of them the new name. The important
part is the pair in the middle: `Ctrl-O` then `.`. Because `Ctrl-O`
restores the exact column, the cursor is back inside the word and `.`
repeats the whole `ciw` change without you locating anything.

This is a two-site rename. For six sites you would reach for `:%s`,
which chapter 14 gave you. For two or three sites in different parts of
a file, jump, change, `Ctrl-O`, dot is faster than typing the
substitute command and does not risk touching a fourth site you had
not noticed.

@start retry.config.ts
export const MAX_RETRIES = 3;

export const retryDelaysMs = [250, 500, 1000, 2000, 4000];

export function delayFor(attempt: number) {
  return retryDelaysMs[Math.min(attempt, retryDelaysMs.length - 1)];
}

export function shouldRetry(attempt: number, status: number) {
  if (status < 500) {
    return false;
  }

  return attempt < MAX_RETRIES;
}

@expected retry.config.ts
export const RETRY_LIMIT = 3;

export const retryDelaysMs = [250, 500, 1000, 2000, 4000];

export function delayFor(attempt: number) {
  return retryDelaysMs[Math.min(attempt, retryDelaysMs.length - 1)];
}

export function shouldRetry(attempt: number, status: number) {
  if (status < 500) {
    return false;
  }

  return attempt < RETRY_LIMIT;
}
